# What is deliberately NOT tracked, and why.
#
# The point of this repository is provenance for CODE and for the ARTIFACTS a
# claim rests on -- the JSON and Markdown that src/make_summary.py reads. Large
# regenerable binaries are excluded: they are 2.4 GB against 14 MB of actual
# results, and /home is already 88% full.

# --- large regenerable binaries -------------------------------------------
# results/sae/*.npz          ~1.8 GB  activation collection + two dictionaries
# results/acts/*.npz         ~510 MB  probe activation caches
# All are rebuilt by `bash run_full_pipeline.sh` stage 8 and by probe.py.
*.npz

# ...except the trained constraint-layer adapters. They are 1.1 MB each, they
# are the actual deliverable of Aim 3, and every constraint-layer row in every
# table is scored with one. Losing them means retraining to reproduce a number.
!results/adapter_*.npz

# --- third-party source corpora -------------------------------------------
# MedCalc-Bench CSVs, 54 MB, redistributed by their own authors under their own
# licence. src/build_medcalc.py reads them; they are not ours to vendor.
data/external/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The UMLS and openFDA keys live in ../.env, outside this tree. These patterns
# are belt-and-braces: BACKLOG.md section 5 records that keys have been pasted
# into a chat before, so the cost of one leaking again is not hypothetical.
.env
*.key
*.pem
secrets.*

# --- generated state -------------------------------------------------------
.pipeline_state/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# --- archives --------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
data/mimic_demo/
